gomodel:6ab067da00011397
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "XIAP is modelled with signaling adaptor activity (GO:0035591). PMID:35263589 shows only that EXTL3 binds XIAP and XIAP binds BCL10 (Fig. 6C) and that XIAP knockdown abolishes the Reg3g effect (Fig. 6D). The function is inferred from binding plus knockdown; XIAP's established MF is E3 ubiquitin ligase activity, which this paper does not test in this pathway." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. Nociceptor-derived Reg3g suppresses the microglial kynurenine pathway, lowering quinolinate and preserving c-Src-dependent HK1 phosphorylation and neuronal ATP production during endotoxemia (PMID:35263589)." , "Quinolinate (CHEBI:29959) is not the direct product of any activity in this model. HAAO outputs cis,cis-2-amino-3-carboxymuconate 6-semialdehyde (CHEBI:77612, RHEA:17953), which cyclises to quinolinate spontaneously. There is no enzyme and therefore no activity unit for that step; the quinolinate node represents its product, and the HAAO -> SRC causal edge carries the biology (PMID:35263589 Fig. 3I, S4A-S4E)." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "production" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-26" ;
        dc:title               "Nociceptor-derived Reg3g suppresses the microglial kynurenine pathway and protects neuronal ATP production in endotoxemia (Mouse)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00011397 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_10090 .

